# promise: #741
# A click on the Picture in Picture window with another app in front brings Cra forward, as Arc 1.173.1's does, so a
# pinch after it resizes the window. macOS gives a trackpad pinch only to the app in front, and Cra's window is a
# non-activating panel (#206): a click left Cra behind and the pinch went nowhere (Arc's own window doesn't take a
# pinch before that click either). Cra comes forward without its browser windows, which stay behind the app the user
# was in, and an automatic Picture in Picture's video stays out (CraCore PictureInPictureFront). A test copy stays
# behind the user's apps, so here the decision is read in the log: the copy is in the background, and the click
# brings it forward.
budget rss=900 stalls50=20
cra://open?url=file://${FIXTURES}/Pages/video.html
expect-log loaded file:
wait 2
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"document.getElementById('v').requestPictureInPicture().then(()=>'pip:open')","awaitPromise":true,"userGesture":true}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*"value":"pip:open"
wait 1
cra://debug?pipSize=0.30
expect-log pip: resized to
wait 1
reject-log pip: a press on the window brings Cra forward
cra://debug?pipClick=1
expect-log pip: a press on the window brings Cra forward \(#741\)
wait 1
# The pinch itself, as before (#534).
cra://debug?pipPinch=0.1,0.1,0.1
expect-log pip: pinched [0-9]+×[0-9]+ → [0-9]+×[0-9]+
